Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_BONUS_JETEYE_PEDIA	Jeteye is an addictive drug that sedates and can cause horrible hallucinations. It is administered by squirting the liquid inside the eyelid, and can turn the entire iris and sclera of the user black. The source of the drug is a bit of a mystery, but the leading theory is that it is produced from the ink of Krakens.[PARAGRAPH:2]After Auric is banished to the Netherworl, the Nether Blade is stored in the Bay of Laurus. Os-Gabella ends up traveling to the city to attempt to find it and use it to end her immortal life. Before she does so she discovers the Jeteye dealers of the cities ports and finds some measure of escape in the delusions and opiate dreams the drug offers. Somewhere among the cities beggars the first human lives in squalor, once queen of the Sheaim, once grandmother to the Calabim, once unwilling bride to the god Nemed, her world is now little more than visions and dancing shadows. More than one man seeking to abuse or hurt the cities beggers has met his end when he assumed Os-Gabella was just another broken vagrant. 	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_BONUS_MANA_AIR_PEDIA	[TAB]Allows access to the Air sphere spells:[NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_FAIR_WINDS]Fair Winds[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_AIR1]Air I[\\LINK] or [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_AIR]Air Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING1]Channeling I[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_MAELSTROM]Maelstrom[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_AIR2]Air II[\\LINK] or [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_AIR]Air Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING2]Channeling II[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_SUMMON_AIR_ELEMENTAL]Summon Air Elemental[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_AIR3]Air III[\\LINK] or [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_AIR]Air Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING3]Channeling III[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_TEMPEST]Tempest[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_AIR]Air Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING4]Channeling IV[\\LINK][PARAGRAPH][PARAGRAPH]The more sources of this Mana you control, the more likely your [LINK=UNITCOMBAT_ADEPT]Arcane units[\\LINK] are to be gifted with [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_AIR]Affinity for this sphere[\\LINK]. That not only increases the unit's strength based on how much mana you control, but lets it learn more powerful versions of the spells in this sphere for free, without spending any xp to level up, so long as it has the proper Channeling promotions. [PARAGRAPH]The effective supply of Air Mana is greater for the [LINK=CIVILIZATION_HIPPUS]Hippus[\\LINK] civilization and for those following [LINK=RELIGION_FOXMEN]The Foxmen[\\LINK]. It is reduced for those following [LINK=RELIGION_RUNES_OF_KILMORPH]The Runes of Kilmorph[\\LINK], either as a State Religion or as the caster's personal faith. [PARAGRAPH:2]Air is the sphere of disregarding consequences and responsibilities in order to just have fun in the moment. The One intended for this sphere to balance out the sphere of Earth, which deals with being responsible. Air is one of the chaotic spheres, which can be considered chaos without malevolence. The ideology of this sphere may be represented as a group of men settings off to paint a random building red, but they get distracted, paint a bull and twelve geese red then spend the night taking care of the geese because they can't fly anymore with paint on them, and then they cook and eat 2 of the geese when they get hungry, paint each other red and wander back into the city the next morning red and covered in goose feathers. [PARAGRAPH]Tali is the God of Air. He does not have the patience for organized religion, but does favor a group of the [LINK=UNIT_PRIEST_FOXMEN]wandering[\\LINK] worshipers known as [LINK=RELIGION_FOXMEN]the Foxmen[\\LINK]. They tend to be daredevils, for whom adventure is the greatest form of worship. They have no temples, but do maintain several small shrines in remote locations such as the edges of the highest cliffs in the world. When Foxmen cross paths on their journeys, they like to share a drink up on the rooftops of the local Inns and Taverns. 	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_BONUS_MANA_BODY_PEDIA	[TAB]Allows access to the Body sphere spells:[NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_HASTE]Haste[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_BODY1]Body I[\\LINK] or [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_BODY]Body Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING1]Channeling I[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_REGENERATION]Regeneration[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_BODY2]Body II[\\LINK] or [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_BODY]Body Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING2]Channeling II[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_STRENGTHEN]Strengthen[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_BODY3]Body III[\\LINK] or [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_BODY]Body Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING3]Channeling III[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_CREATE_CHIMERA]Create Chimera[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_BODY]Body Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING4]Channeling IV[\\LINK][PARAGRAPH][PARAGRAPH]The more sources of this Mana you control, the more likely your [LINK=UNITCOMBAT_ADEPT]Arcane units[\\LINK] are to be gifted with [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_BODY]Affinity for this sphere[\\LINK]. That not only increases the unit's strength based on how much mana you control, but lets it learn more powerful versions of the spells in this sphere for free, without spending any xp to level up, so long as it has the proper Channeling promotions. [PARAGRAPH]The effective supply of Body Mana is greater for the [LINK=CIVILIZATION_CALABIM]Calabim[\\LINK] civilization. [PARAGRAPH:2]Body is the sphere of strength. It was supposed to assist the sphere of Spirit and allow the strong to protect the weak, but since the fall of Aeron the strong have preferred to assert their dominance and oppress the weak. It has become the sphere of rage and the basest of passions. It is however not wild and uncontrolled, but cold and calculating. Aeron is the God of Murder, the patron of assassins and psychopaths. 	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_BONUS_MANA_CREATION	Creation Mana	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_BONUS_MANA_CREATION_PEDIA	[TAB]The more of this resource you control the more likely your arcane units are to be gifted with [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_CREATION]Creation Affinity[\\LINK]. This sphere is unique in that its affinity may be even granted to [LINK=UNIT_ADEPT]Adepts[\\LINK] with no experience rather than being reserved for those who have reached level 3 and been upgraded to Mages. It is also unique in that it does not have any promotions that may be learned with experience when a unit levels up. There are no lesser and greater versions of its spells. [PARAGRAPH]Creation affinity allows access to the Creation sphere spells:[NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_MUSE]Muse[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_SUMMON_PIXIE]Summon Pixie[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING2]Channeling II[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_ABUNDANCE]Abundance[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING3]Channeling III[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_REJUVENATE]Rejuvenate[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING3]Channeling IV[\\LINK][PARAGRAPH:2]The effective supply of Creation Mana is greater for the [LINK=CIVILIZATION_KURIOTATES]Kuriotates[\\LINK] civilization or those following [LINK=RELIGION_HOUSE_OF_PLENTY]The House of Plenty[\\LINK]. It is reduced for those following [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ASHEN_VEIL]The Ashen Veil[\\LINK], either as a State Religion or as the caster's personal faith. [PARAGRAPH:2]Creation is the sphere of new beginnings, births, and inspiration. It is about original ideas and the emergence of unexpected order out of creative chaos. The One intended for Creation to be the compliment of Hope. Hope longs for a particular outcome, drives us to work towards it, and may lead to despair if its aim seems unattainable. Creation prefers to remain open to unexpected possibilities, which often turns out better than fixating on what we thought we wanted. [PARAGRAPH]Amathaon presides over this sphere. He is a gentle soul who loves little children and hates conflict. He wanted nothing to do with the Godswar, but knew that the forces of his sphere must marshal in order to stop Agares from destroying Erebus out of spite. Rather than personally fight, he invented the weapon of mass destruction that came to define the age: The Dragon. Other gods soon copied him and created many such beasts to serve them, but all paled in comparison to [LINK=UNIT_EURABATRES]Eurabatres the Golden Dragon[\\LINK]. The first true dragon was the greatest being ever created since The One made the gods themselves. [PARAGRAPH]Whereas most gods favor their worshipers, Amathaon shows no such partiality. He instead shows caprice, sharing his blessings seemingly at random. Most Creation Mages do not even know they are mages. 	
Magister_CIV4GameText_FFH2.xml	TXT_KEY_BONUS_MANA_CHAOS_PEDIA	[TAB]Allows access to the Chaos sphere spells:[NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_SPELL_DANCE_OF_BLADES]Dance of Blades[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_CHAOS1]Chaos I[\\LINK] or [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_CHAOS]Chaos Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING1]Channeling I[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_SUMMON_PIT_BEAST]Summon Pit Beast[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_CHAOS2]Chaos II[\\LINK] or [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_CHAOS]Chaos Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING2]Channeling II[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_WONDER]Wonder[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_CHAOS]Chaos III[\\LINK] or [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_CHAOS]Chaos Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING3]Channeling III[\\LINK][NEWLINE][TAB][ICON_BULLET][LINK=SPELL_MUTATION]Mutation[\\LINK] with [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_CHAOS]Chaos Affinity[\\LINK] and [LINK=PROMOTION_CHANNELING4]Channeling IV[\\LINK][PARAGRAPH][PARAGRAPH]The more sources of this Mana you control, the more likely your [LINK=UNITCOMBAT_ADEPT]Arcane units[\\LINK] are to be gifted with [LINK=PROMOTION_AFFINITY_CHAOS]Affinity for this sphere[\\LINK]. That not only increases the unit's strength based on how much mana you control, but lets it learn more powerful versions of the spells in this sphere for free, without spending any xp to level up, so long as it has the proper Channeling promotions.[PARAGRAPH]The effective supply of Chaos Mana is greater for the [LINK=CIVILIZATION_DOVIELLO]Doviello[\\LINK] civilization or for those following [LINK=RELIGION_SONS_OF_DISCORD]The Sons of Discord[\\LINK]. It is reduced for those following [LINK=RELIGION_THE_ORDER]The Order[\\LINK], either as a State Religion or as the caster's personal faith. [PARAGRAPH:2]Chaos was created to be the sphere of interpersonal Peace, but has become the sphere of Strife. Camulos's individualism was created to balance Junil's insistence that we conform to external authorities. He was always an Anarchist, but originally focused on preventing individuals from constraining the freedom of others. Now he prefers to free men from the constraints of conscience and insists that everyone has the right to abuse everyone else. He exercises little to no control even in own vault, which has become an eternal battleground where a myriad demons vie for ephemeral dominance. He has no organized religion, but there are several underground cults devoted to this God of War. He tends to answer prayers with curses. When his most famed worshiper during the Age of Magic, [LINK=UNIT_DUIN]Baron Duin Halfmorn[\\LINK], prayed to Camulos for more followers, he made him a Lycanthrope. Gods rarely release the souls they have claimed, but Camulos sent the souls of both Duin and [LINK=LEADER_CHARADON]Charadon[\\LINK] back to Erebus in the Age of Rebirth to cause more strife. 	
